rted shifting toward using GPUs to render movies, because modern professional GPUs (which cost tens of thousands of dollars each) finally have enough memory and power to handle it. ### Summary You are completely correct that computers are rendering the movie. But the reason it feels like your PC can play a movie "so easily" compared to a game is because **your** graphics card is just pressing "play" on a video file. The actual rendering was done months ago by a warehouse full of supercomputers that took hours to calculate a single second of footage!
